From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini station: enable the sensor bus

Enable I2C1, on GPIO55/56 as the board's pin table sets them, at the 400 kHz
the vendor kernel runs it. Enable the existing BMI160 node at 0x69 and add the
STK3x1x light and proximity sensor at 0x48, with its interrupt on GPIO88 as
EINT11.

The vendor's boot log has "Flags mismatch irq 395 (bmi160_accint) vs (ALS-eint)".
That is the vendor IMU driver looking up the light sensor's node and asking for
its line with another trigger, not a shared wire, and the same driver programs
none of the IMU's interrupt pins. So the line stays the light sensor's alone
and the IMU has none. The upstream driver reads without one.

Enabling the bus sends nothing on it. Both drivers are modules nothing loads.

Name no supplies. The vendor drives no rail for these parts and its power
fields hold a "none" placeholder, so the rails are expected to be up, as they
are for the vendor kernel.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 .../mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts    | 44 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -504,3 +504,47 @@
 		linux,guard-end-threshold = <80>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * The sensor bus. Nothing on it is touched until a sensor module loads, and
+ * nothing loads them. The vendor kernel runs this bus at 400 kHz. No supplies:
+ * the vendor manages none, and its description of them is a placeholder.
+ */
+&pio {
+	stk3311_pins: stk3311-pins {
+		pins-irq {
+			pinmux = <MT6797_GPIO88__FUNC_EINT11>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c1 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&i2c1_pins_a>;
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	/*
+	 * Product ID 0x11 is not one the driver names. It warns and carries on,
+	 * and the vendor driver treats it as a generic part of this family. The
+	 * pin's pull-up, which the vendor selects, cannot be set: the MT6797 pin
+	 * data has no pull registers, so the pad stays as the firmware left it.
+	 */
+	light-sensor@48 {
+		compatible = "sensortek,stk3311";
+		reg = <0x48>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&stk3311_pins>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&pio>;
+		interrupts = <11 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * No interrupt. The vendor IMU driver asks for the light sensor's line, by
+ * looking up that sensor's node, and fails with a flags mismatch; it programs
+ * none of the chip's interrupt pins. So no pin is known to be the IMU's.
+ */
+&bmi160_candidate {
+	status = "okay";
+};
